{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/30756-custom-were-critters","id":30756,"title":"Custom were-critters?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-15T21:15:33-08:00","id":30756,"title":"Custom were-critters?","content":"What is the best splat for creating a custom were-whatever in nWoD? I recall there was some debate between two books. It's been a few years. I remember the one I used had some oddities (like the primal urge scale was totally different from every other published werecritter).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T21:45:15-08:00","id":30769,"title":"","content":"Changing Breeds is the not-good one; instead use the material from Skinchangers and/or the fourth chapter of War Against the Pure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T21:59:29-08:00","id":30774,"title":"","content":"Thanks kindly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T00:10:26-08:00","id":30804,"title":"","content":"I agree with using War Against the Pure. So much more unique and fitting then Changing Breeds was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Things need not have happened to be true. Tales and dreams are the shadow truths that will endure when mere facts are dust and ashes, and forgot.&quot; Sandman (Neil Gaiman)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/733-troller","name":"Troller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T07:24:59-08:00","id":33163,"title":"","content":"I often create mine on the fly, I am currently using the crow host in my games and when players come across a new power scale I simply adjust the gauru attributes.<br /> <br /> I.E. Strength +3 Stamina +2 Dexterity +1 for gauru.<br /> Therefore +3 Intelligence +2 Resolve +1 Wits for my more intellect based crow hosts in gauru.<br /> <br /> For more info though Skinchangers is an awesome read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1387-moxy","name":"Moxy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1387_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T18:23:56-08:00","id":33590,"title":"","content":"Definitely War Against the Pure's section for me (though Skinchangers I get some some good mileage from). I've got a Camazotz Were-Vampire bat tied heavily to Xilbalba (and specifically -not- derived from anything Shadow related rather than the Underworld; yep, that catches folks off guard) that are created from old Mayan sacrificial altars. House of Bats and all that, auspices tied to the dualistic deities of Xilbalba (like the flying scab). I found the Aspects in WatP to work quite well; Flight, Echolocation; mix in some Gifts-as-Aspects from the Blood gift-set, a smattering of stuff from Death and heart-eating and voil\u00e0. Definitely a very versatile chapter, and a couple of the example shifters (the Brine-Born and the Unclean I think they were called) caught my eye too.<br /> <br /> I'll pipe up with the rest though; don't waste your time with Changing Breeds. It's a mechanically borked, poorly written mess. If you've got a hankering for an nWoD redux of the old W:tA Bastet (seriously), you might find something in there, but you're much better off with the other two books. It has the saving grace of what seems to be a decent size chart for animals. Not much else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T10:40:14-08:00","id":33956,"title":"","content":"One of my players wrote up a faction of werelions with some really good fluff, and I wanted to reward the extra effort with making them playable for her. Skinchangers don't really fit, since they aren't innate shapeshifters and need a talisman, though I love some of the mechanics and may use them for NPCs and antagonists.<br /> <br /> My problem with War Against the Pure is they don't seem to balance well against regular Werewolves, since they're basically Werewolves minus some of the abilities Werewolves get as far as I could tell?<br /> <br /> At least, in play she seemed to lag behind other players despite getting more bonus XP for roleplaying well.<br /> <br /> Any tips for making sure a War Against the Pure werecreature doesn't lag behind balance-wise? Anything I may have done that caused it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T10:49:10-08:00","id":33959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/30756-custom-were-critters?p=33956#post33956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Skinchangers don't really fit, since they aren't innate shapeshifters and need a talisman</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026Okay, now I'm confused. Talisman-based shifting is one of the things in Skinchangers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T20:32:16-08:00","id":34270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/30756-custom-were-critters?p=33959#post33959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026Okay, now I'm confused. Talisman-based shifting is one of the things in Skinchangers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the awkward sentence structure. Skinchangers doesn't fit because skinchangers aren't innate shapeshifters and require a talisman. The fluff the player wrote for me works more like a standard werewolf, where it's more or less innate. Genetics more than external magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T22:13:02-08:00","id":34297,"title":"","content":"Definitely War Against the Pure then as that's certainly one a few options presented on how they come to be.<br /> <br /> And you're right, the creation system in there does, for PC's at least, fall short of your average Werewolf PC. It's much like Purified and main-line splats; the Aspects build short changes them a bit. If you want more mileage, the best bet is to adapt something like Instincts (be it from the Chronicler's Guide, or something like the custom home-brew I've been working on with others if you peek at the sig) or the most appropriate Gift Lists as affinity, and allow them to be purchased like a Forsaken.<br /> <br /> Up the basic abilities to reflect what Werewolves get (loci sensing, stepping sideways, blood-based hunting bonuses, the -benefits- of Death Rage as a survival mechanism, Regeneration, 5 forms, Rites etc.) so they aren't as far behind in their own tidbits, give them some choice picks of Rites that may make sense and they won't be doing as badly.<br /> <br /> The only consistent issue that comes up is Renown; you may need to substitute the dice pools they use for something like 1/2 Primal Urge (rounding up) or similar given their lack of it with how some Gifts run if you don't do some tinkering. I'm honestly not quite sure why the shifters in that book are short-changed out of the gate; they're not -that- badly behind at least, but late mid-to-late game they definitely fall short.<br /> <br /> Luckily it's not difficult to fix, mostly some mild tweaking. If you're playing around with a spirit-heavy game, make sure they don't get dinked during creation having to buy Shadow-related Aspects on top of everything else if it covers basic capacity to deal with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}